asgard-gnome-desktop (1.0.1) thor; urgency=low

  * Ship /etc/NetworkManager/conf.d/10-asgard-managed.conf carrying
    `[ifupdown] managed=true`.  Without it, NetworkManager defers to
    ifupdown on any interface listed in /etc/network/interfaces (the
    installer leaves a DHCP entry there for the install-time
    interface), GNOME Shell sees zero NM-managed devices, and the
    top-bar network indicator never appears.  Postinst restarts NM
    so the drop-in takes effect immediately on `apt install` without
    requiring a reboot.
  * Make network-manager an explicit Depends (was transitive via
    network-manager-gnome) so the metapackage's dependency graph
    documents the relationship a reader expects.

 -- Athena Build <athena@local>  Tue, 02 Jun 2026 01:22:00 +0000

asgard-gnome-desktop (1.0.0) thor; urgency=low

  * Initial @DISTRIBUTION@ metapackage for the GNOME desktop group.
    Mirrors config/pkg.list [gnome-desktop] seed list verbatim so
    `apt install asgard-gnome-desktop` on a booted system pulls the
    same closure tasksel's GNOME Desktop task installs at first boot.
    Pattern B per docs/branding-methodology.md — coexists with the
    pkg.list group and the tasksel Key list; does not replace either.

 -- Athena Build <athena@local>  Mon, 01 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
